# Finding B in Garnet 2.2.14 (RESULTS.md, "The three failures traced"); seed 89 of the second
# exploration. A pause of g1 before steps 12 to 15 moves the moment of the failover. The
# composition moves slot 13404 from g3 to g1 and fails shard 3 over to g6 before gossip has told
# g6 of the migration. g6 takes over the slots of its own stale slot map, 13404 among them, with
# the config epoch of g1's claim, so g1 and g6 both serve the slot and both acknowledge writes of
# it. The failover of shard 1 to g4 gives the slot back to shard 1, and the two writes that g6
# acknowledged stay on g6 and g3. The cause of finding 2, on the source's side.
# params: device=FileStream reest=5
# commands: anytime_read first_init parallel_driver_del parallel_driver_hset parallel_driver_incr parallel_driver_lua parallel_driver_over parallel_driver_rpush parallel_driver_sadd parallel_driver_set parallel_driver_setex parallel_driver_txn parallel_driver_zadd serial_driver_failover serial_driver_migrate serial_driver_save
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=none dseed=0 | run P=g1@12+3 W=0a39fa3d,p1,q2,r500
